          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Rozansky-Witten weight systems are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+systems"} weight systems
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+diagrams"} Jacobi diagrams
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chord+diagrams+modulo+4T+are+Jacobi+diagrams+modulo+STU"} equivalently
            on
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/round+chord+diagrams"} round chord diagrams
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rozansky-Witten+invariants"} Rozansky-Witten invariants
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} hyperkähler manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dolbeault+cohomology"} Dolbeault cohomology
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+groups"} groups
          %p
            For asymptotically flat and for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} compact hyperkähler manifolds
            the induced RW-weight systems take values in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            and hence are actual
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+systems"} weight systems
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            Rozansky-Witten weight systems depend only on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifold"} hyperkähler manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}^{4n}
            which is the (classical)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coulomb+branch"} Coulomb branch
            of the RW-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+twist"} twisted
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D3+N%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=3 N=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+geometry"} Riemannian geometry
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}^{4n}
            and depend only on the underlying holomorphic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+structure"} symplectic structure
            (
            %a{:href => "#Kapranov99"}> Kapranov 99
            ). Generally, they are defined for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}^{4n}
            any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifold"} hyperkähler manifold
            which is either asymptotically flat (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ALE+spaces"}> ALE spaces
            ) or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact topological space
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifolds"}> compact hyperkähler manifolds
            ).
          %p
            Via the equivalent reformulation by
            %a{:href => "#Kapranov99"} Kapranov 99
            one finds (
            %a{:href => "#RobertsWillerton10"}> Roberts-Willerton 10
            ) that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rozansky-Witten+invariants"} Rozansky-Witten invariants
            are structurally
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+weight+systems"} Lie algebra weight systems
            themselves, but
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+object"} internal
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category+of+coherent+sheaves"} derived category of coherent sheaves
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}^{4n}
            and composed with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration"} integration
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}^{4n}
            which makes the resulting
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dolbeault+cohomology"} Dolbeault cohomology
            = succeed "-valued." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#groundfield_valued_weight_systems Ground-field valued weight systems
          %p
            In order for Rozansky-Witten weight systems to take values in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+systems"} weight systems
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifold"} hyperkähler manifold
            has to be asymptotically flat or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            (i.e.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} compact hyperkähler manifolds
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+schemes+of+points"} Hilbert schemes of points
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{[n+1]}
            (for
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            either
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surface"} K3-surface
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-torus"} 4-torus
                (in which case the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+hyperk%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} compact hyperkähler manifolds
                is really the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝕋
                          %mn 4
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝕋
                          %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{T}^4)^{[n]} \to \mathbb{T}^4
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "compact+hyperkähler+manifold#Beauville83"}> Beauville 83
            ) and two exceptional examples (
            %a{:href => "compact+hyperkähler+manifold#OGrady99"}> O’Grady 99
            ,
            %a{:href => "compact+hyperkähler+manifold#OGrady03"} O’Grady 03
            ), see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "compact+hyperkähler+manifold#Sawon04"} Sawon 04, Sec. 5.3
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D3+N%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=3 N=4 super Yang-Mills theory
          %div
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chord+diagrams"} chord diagrams
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+systems"} weight systems
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+chord+diagrams"}> linear chord diagrams
                    ,
                    %br/
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/round+chord+diagrams"} round chord diagrams
                    %br/
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+diagrams"} Jacobi diagrams
                    %br/
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+chord+diagrams"} Sullivan chord diagrams
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+weight+systems"}> Lie algebra weight systems
                    ,
                    %br/
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stringy+weight+system"} stringy weight system
                    %br/
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rozansky-Witten+weight+systems"} Rozansky-Witten weight systems
            %p
              %br/
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/knots"} knots
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braids"} braids
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chord+diagram"}> chord diagram
                    ,
                    %br/
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+diagram"} Jacobi diagram
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagram"} horizontal chord diagram
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1T+relation"}> 1T
                    \&amp;
                    %a{:href => "4T+relation#ForCircularChordDiagrams"} 4T relation
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2T+relation"}> 2T
                    \&amp;
                    %a{:href => "4T+relation#ForHorizontalChordDiagrams"}> 4T relation
                    \/
                    %br/
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+braid+relations"} infinitesimal braid relations
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+system"} weight system
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
